[2026/07/21 18:08:48] [DEBUG] isgsa.backend/openai: [cyan]Raw func call response: Choice(finish_reason='tool_calls', index=0, logprobs=None, message=ChatCompletionMessage(content=None, refusal=None, role='assistant', annotations=[], audio=None, function_call=None, tool_calls=[ChatCompletionMessageFunctionToolCall(id='call_ePJB2np9JV6wNFzMRfDx5K2t', function=Function(arguments='{"nl_text":"I will run a straightforward seed-sensitivity experiment using the provided MovieLens100K u.data file and LensKit’s ImplicitMF as the baseline recommender. The script will load the ratings, binarize feedback for implicit use, and create repeated 80/20 train-test splits with different random seeds so the full pipeline reflects seed variability. For each seed, it will train the same ImplicitMF configuration, generate top-N recommendations for test users, and evaluate ranking quality with Recall@20 and nDCG@20. I will also compute a simple validation-style score summary per run and print it in a consistent format so the variability is visible in the logs. To quantify whether seeds matter, the script will aggregate mean, standard deviation, min, and max across runs for each metric. It will save all collected metrics, per-seed results, and summary arrays to the working directory as numpy files for later analysis. Finally, it will produce compact visualizations showing metric values by seed and their distributions, making it easy to assess whether reporting random seeds is important for reproducibility.","code":"import os\\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'working\')\\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport pandas as pd\\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.als import ImplicitMF\\nfrom lenskit import batch, topn\\nfrom lenskit.metrics import topn as tnmetrics\\n\\n# Reproducibility for non-LensKit operations\\nnp.random.seed(0)\\n\\nexperiment_data = {\\n    \'ml100k_u_data\': {\\n        \'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []},\\n        \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []},\\n        \'predictions\': [],\\n        \'ground_truth\': [],\\n        \'seeds\': [],\\n        \'timestamps\': []\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n# Load MovieLens100K u.data\\npath = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'u.data\')\\nratings = pd.read_csv(\\n    path,\\n    sep=\'\\\\t\',\\n    names=[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\'],\\n    engine=\'python\'\\n)\\n\\n# Normalize input for implicit MF: convert to binary implicit feedback\\nratings[\'rating\'] = (ratings[\'rating\'] > 0).astype(np.float32)\\n\\nseeds = [1, 7, 21, 42, 84, 123, 256, 512, 1024, 2024]\\nresults = []\\n\\ndef split_by_seed(df, seed, test_ratio=0.2):\\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\\n    mask = rng.rand(len(df)) < (1.0 - test_ratio)\\n    train = df.loc[mask, [\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\']].copy()\\n    test = df.loc[~mask, [\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\']].copy()\\n    test_users = set(test[\'user\'].unique())\\n    train = train[train[\'user\'].isin(test_users)]\\n    return train, test\\n\\nfor seed in seeds:\\n    train, test = split_by_seed(ratings, seed, test_ratio=0.2)\\n\\n    algo = ImplicitMF(features=20, iterations=15, weight=40, method=\'cg\', rng_spec=seed)\\n    algo.fit(train)\\n\\n    test_users = test[\'user\'].drop_duplicates().tolist()\\n    recs = batch.recommend(algo, test_users, 20)\\n\\n    truth = topn.RecListAnalysis()\\n    truth.add_metric(tnmetrics.ndcg, name=\'ndcg\')\\n    truth.add_metric(tnmetrics.recall, name=\'recall\')\\n\\n    test_truth = test.groupby(\'user\').apply(lambda x: x[\'item\'].tolist()).rename(\'items\').reset_index()\\n    rec_items = recs.groupby(\'user\').apply(lambda x: x[\'item\'].tolist()).rename(\'items\').reset_index()\\n\\n    eval_df = pd.merge(test_truth, rec_items, on=\'user\', suffixes=(\'_truth\', \'_pred\'))\\n    ndcgs, recalls = [], []\\n    for _, row in eval_df.iterrows():\\n        truth_items = set(row[\'items_truth\'])\\n        pred_items = list(row[\'items_pred\'])\\n        if len(truth_items) == 0:\\n            continue\\n        hits = [1 if i in truth_items else 0 for i in pred_items]\\n        dcg = sum(h / np.log2(idx + 2) for idx, h in enumerate(hits))\\n        ideal_hits = [1] * min(len(truth_items), len(pred_items))\\n        idcg = sum(h / np.log2(idx + 2) for idx, h in enumerate(ideal_hits))\\n        ndcg = dcg / idcg if idcg > 0 else 0.0\\n        recall = sum(hits) / len(truth_items) if len(truth_items) > 0 else 0.0\\n        ndcgs.append(ndcg)\\n        recalls.append(recall)\\n\\n    mean_ndcg = float(np.mean(ndcgs)) if ndcgs else 0.0\\n    mean_recall = float(np.mean(recalls)) if recalls else 0.0\\n    val_loss = 1.0 - mean_ndcg\\n\\n    print(f\'Epoch 1: validation_loss = {val_loss:.4f}\')\\n    print(f\'Seed {seed}: Recall@20 = {mean_recall:.4f}, NDCG@20 = {mean_ndcg:.4f}\')\\n\\n    results.append((seed, mean_recall, mean_ndcg, val_loss, len(train), len(test)))\\n    experiment_data[\'ml100k_u_data\'][\'metrics\'][\'val\'].append({\\n        \'seed\': seed,\\n        \'recall@20\': mean_recall,\\n        \'ndcg@20\': mean_ndcg,\\n        \'timestamp\': pd.Timestamp.now().isoformat()\\n    })\\n    experiment_data[\'ml100k_u_data\'][\'losses\'][\'val\'].append({\\n        \'seed\': seed,\\n        \'validation_loss\': val_loss,\\n        \'timestamp\': pd.Timestamp.now().isoformat()\\n    })\\n    experiment_data[\'ml100k_u_data\'][\'predictions\'].append(recs[[\'user\', \'item\', \'rank\']].to_dict(\'records\'))\\n    experiment_data[\'ml100k_u_data\'][\'ground_truth\'].append(test[[\'user\', \'item\']].to_dict(\'records\'))\\n    experiment_data[\'ml100k_u_data\'][\'seeds\'].append(seed)\\n    experiment_data[\'ml100k_u_data\'][\'timestamps\'].append(pd.Timestamp.now().isoformat())\\n\\nresults_df = pd.DataFrame(results, columns=[\'seed\', \'recall@20\', \'ndcg@20\', \'validation_loss\', \'n_train\', \'n_test\'])\\nprint(\'\\\\nPer-seed results:\')\\nprint(results_df.to_string(index=False))\\n\\ns