[2026/07/21 18:13:10] [DEBUG] isgsa.llm: prompt content: {'Instructions': 'You are an expert recommender system researcher conducting a code review for an important experiment. You are provided the research task, the code implementation and the execution output. You must score the code using the following requirements: \n1. Load MovieLens100K ratings from the local `u.data` file in the current working directory using the correct tab-separated schema: user id, item id, rating, timestamp.\n2. Use LensKit’s ImplicitMF recommender with a fixed configuration for all runs; only the random seed may vary across repeated trainings.\n3. Create a single 80/20 train/test split of the ratings data and keep that split identical across all seed runs so seed effects are isolated to model randomness, not data splitting randomness.\n4. Ensure all other stochastic sources are controlled or fixed where possible (e.g., split seed, evaluation candidate generation, NumPy/Python random state if relevant) so the experiment measures training-seed variability.\n5. Train the model multiple times with different random seeds; use enough runs to estimate variability meaningfully (at least 10 distinct seeds, preferably more).\n6. Generate top-N recommendations for each test user using the same recommendation cutoff `N` in every run.\n7. Evaluate each run with ranking metrics appropriate to the task, including at minimum NDCG and Recall; compute metrics consistently on the same test users/items across runs.\n8. Store per-run results in a structured table containing at least: seed, metric values, and any key run settings needed for reproducibility.\n9. Summarize seed sensitivity quantitatively across runs using statistics such as mean, standard deviation, min, max, and coefficient of variation or confidence intervals for each metric.\n10. Report the absolute and relative spread of metric values across seeds and identify whether differences are practically noticeable compared with the mean performance.\n11. Include basic validation checks so the script fails clearly if `u.data` is missing, malformed, or if evaluation produces empty user sets or NaN metrics.\n12. Make the experiment fully reproducible by explicitly recording the train/test split procedure, all model hyperparameters, all seeds used, package versions if available, and the exact evaluation protocol.\n13. Present a concise conclusion from the observed metric variability addressing the research question of whether random seeds materially affect results enough that reporting seeds is important.\n. Each requirement can either be fullfilled or not fulfilled. The score is the percentage of requirements that are fulfilled, e.g. if 7 out of 10 requirements are fulfilled, the score is 70. Additionally, you provide clear and constructive feedback how to improve the code implementation based on the requirements.', 'Research Task': " You are an expert recommender systems research assistant who is looking to help the user with their requests.\nThe user has some idea and you want to conduct creative experiments to gain scientific insights.\nYour aim is to run experiments to gather sufficient results to report back to the user.\nThe idea is:\n\nI'd like to run an experiment to quantify how much random seeds affect recommender system results.\nPlease use a simple ImplicitMF algorithm from LensKit, perform an 80/20 train/test split on the MovieLens100K 'u.data',\ntrain it multiple times with identical settings but different random seeds,\nand analyze how metrics like NDCG or Recall vary across runs to find out if reporting seeds is important.\nI placed the 'u.data' file of MovieLens100K in your current working directory. You can load it from there!", 'Implementation': "```python\nimport os\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), 'working')\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.als import ImplicitMF\nfrom lenskit.algorithms import Recommender\nfrom lenskit import batch\n\nnp.random.seed(0)\n\nexperiment_data = {\n    'ml100k_u_data': {\n        'metrics': {'train': [], 'val': []},\n        'losses': {'train': [], 'val': []},\n        'predictions': [],\n        'ground_truth': [],\n        'seeds': [],\n        'timestamps': [],\n        'split_info': {}\n    }\n}\n\npath = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), 'u.data')\nratings = pd.read_csv(path, sep='\\t', names=['user', 'item', 'rating', 'timestamp'], engine='python')\nratings = ratings[['user', 'item', 'rating']].copy()\nratings['rating'] = (ratings['rating'] > 0).astype(np.float32)\n\ndef fixed_split(df, test_ratio=0.2, seed=2025):\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n    mask = rng.rand(len(df)) < (1.0 - test_ratio)\n    train = df.loc[mask, ['user', 'item', 'rating']].copy()\n    test = df.loc[~mask, ['user', 'item', 'rating']].copy()\n    train_users = set(train['user'].unique())\n    train_items = set(train['item'].unique())\n    test = test[test['user'].isin(train_users) & test['item'].isin(train_items)].copy()\n    user_counts = test.groupby('user').size()\n    valid_users = user_counts[user_counts > 0].index\n    test = test[test['user'].isin(valid_users)].copy()\n    return train.reset_index(drop=True), test.reset_index(drop=True)\n\ndef evaluate_user(truth_items, pred_items, k=20):\n    truth_set = set(truth_items)\n    pred = list(pred_items)[:k]\n    if not truth_set:\n        return None, None\n    hits = [1 if i in truth_set else 0 for i in pred]\n    dcg = sum(h / np.log2(idx + 2) for idx, h in enumerate(hits))\n    idcg = sum(1 / np.log2(idx + 2) for idx in range(min(len(truth_set), len(pred))))\n    ndcg = dcg / idcg if idcg > 0 else 0.0\n    recall = sum(hits) / len(truth_set)\n    return recall, ndcg\n\ntrain, test = fixed_split(ratings, test_ratio=0.2, seed=2025)\nexperiment_data['ml100k_u_data']['split_info'] = {\n    'split_seed': 2025,\n    'n_ratings': int(len(ratings)),\n    'n_train': int(len(train)),\n    'n_test': int(len(test)),\n    'n_train_users': int(train['user'].nunique()),\n    'n_test_users': int(test['user'].nunique()),\n    'n_items': int(ratings['item'].nunique())\n}\n\ntruth_df = test.groupby('user')['item'].apply(list).reset_index(name='items_truth')\ntest_users = truth_df['user'].tolist()\n\nseeds = [1, 7, 21, 42, 84, 123, 256, 512, 1024, 2024]\nresults = []\n\nfor epoch, seed in enumerate(seeds, start=1):\n    base_algo = ImplicitMF(features=20, iterations=15, weight=40, method='cg', rng_spec=seed)\n    algo = Recommender.adapt(base_algo)\n    algo.fit(train)\n\n    recs = batch.recommend(algo, test_users, 20, n_jobs=1)\n    rec_items = recs.groupby('user')['item'].apply(list).reset_index(name='items_pred')\n    eval_df = pd.merge(truth_df, rec_items, on='user', how='inner')\n\n    recalls, ndcgs = [], []\n    for row in eval_df.itertuples(index=False):\n        recall, ndcg = evaluate_user(row.items_truth, row.items_pred, k=20)\n        if recall is not None:\n            recalls.append(recall)\n            ndcgs.append(ndcg)\n\n    mean_recall = float(np.mean(recalls)) if recalls else 0.0\n    mean_ndcg = float(np.mean(ndcgs)) if ndcgs else 0.0\n    val_loss = 1.0 - mean_ndcg\n\n    print(f'Epoch {epoch}: validation_loss = {val_loss:.4f}')\n    print(f'Seed {seed}: Recall@20 = {mean_recall:.4f}, NDCG@20 = {mean_ndcg:.4f}')\n\n    timestamp = pd.Timestamp.now().isoformat()\n    results.append((seed, mean_recall, mean_ndcg, val_loss, len(train), len(test), len(eval_df)))\n    experiment_data['ml100k_u_data']['metrics']['val'].append({\n        'epoch': epoch,\n        'seed': seed,\n        'recall@20': mean_recall,\n        'ndcg@20': mean_ndcg,\n        'timestamp': timestamp\n    })\n    experiment_data['ml100k_u_data']['losses']['val'].append({\n        'epoch': epoch,\n        'seed': seed,\n        'validation_loss': val_loss,\n        'timestamp': timestamp\n    })\n    experiment_data['ml100k_u_data']['predictions'].append(recs[['user', 'item', 'rank']].to_dict('records'))\n    experiment_data['ml100k_u_data']['ground_truth'].append(test[['user', 'item']].to_dict('records'))\n    experiment_data['ml100k_u_data']['seeds'].append(seed)\n    experiment_data['ml100k_u_data']['timestamps'].append(timestamp)\n\nresults_df = pd.DataFrame(results, columns=['seed', 'recall@20', 'ndcg@20', 'validation_loss', 'n_train', 'n_test', 'n_eval_users'])\nprint('\\nPer-seed results:')\nprint(results_df.to_string(index=False))\n\nsummary = results_df[['recall@20', 'ndcg@20', 'validation_loss']].agg(['mean', 'std', 'min', 'max'])\nprint('\\nSummary across seeds:')\nprint(summary)\n\nrecall_vals = results_df['recall@20'].to_numpy()\nndcg_vals = results_df['ndcg@20'].to_numpy()\nloss_vals = results_df['validation_loss'].to_numpy()\nseed_vals = results_df['seed'].to_numpy()\n\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'ml100k_seed_results.npy'), results_df.to_records(index=False))\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'ml100k_recall_at20.npy'), recall_vals)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'ml100k_ndcg_at20.npy'), ndcg_vals)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'ml100k_validation_loss.npy'), loss_vals)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'ml100k_test_truth.npy'), truth_df.to_records(index=False))\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'experiment_data.npy'), experiment_data, allow_pickle=True)\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(10, 4))\nplt.plot(seed_vals, recall_vals, marker='o', label='Recall@20')\nplt.plot(seed_vals, ndcg_vals, marker='s', label='NDCG@20')\nplt.xlabel('Random seed')\nplt.ylabel('Metric value')\nplt.title('MovieLens100K ImplicitMF metrics across seeds (fixed split)')\nplt.legend()\nplt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig(os.path.join(working_dir, 'ml100k_metrics_by_seed.png'), dpi=150)\nplt.close()\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\nplt.boxplot([recall_vals, ndcg_vals], tick_labels=['Recall@20', 'NDCG@20'])\nplt.ylabel('Metric value')\nplt.title('Distribution of metrics across seeds')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig(os.path.join(working_dir, 'ml100k_metric_distribution.png'), dpi=150)\nplt.close()\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\nplt.plot(range(1, len(loss_vals) + 1), loss_vals, marker='d')\nplt.xticks(range(1, len(loss_vals) + 1), seed_vals, rotation=45)\nplt.xlabel('Seed')\nplt.ylabel('Validation loss (1 - NDCG@20)')\nplt.title('Validation loss across seeds')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig(os.path.join(working_dir, 'ml100k_validation_loss_by_seed.png'), dpi=150)\nplt.close()\n\ncv = {\n    'recall@20_cv': float(np.std(recall_vals) / np.mean(recall_vals)) if np.mean(recall_vals) > 0 else 0.0,\n    'ndcg@20_cv': float(np.std(ndcg_vals) / np.mean(ndcg_vals)) if np.mean(ndcg_vals) > 0 else 0.0\n}\nspread = {\n    'recall@20_range': float(np.max(recall_vals) - np.min(recall_vals)) if len(recall_vals) else 0.0,\n    'ndcg@20_range': float(np.max(ndcg_vals) - np.min(ndcg_vals)) if len(ndcg_vals) else 0.0\n}\nprint('\\nCoefficient of variation:')\nprint(cv)\nprint('\\nMetric ranges:')\nprint(spread)\n\nif cv['ndcg@20_cv'] > 0.05 or cv['recall@20_cv'] > 0.05:\n    print('Conclusion: seed effects are non-trivial on a fixed split, so reporting seeds is important.')\nelse:\n    print('Conclusion: seed effects are modest on this fixed split, but reporting seeds remains good practice.')\n\n```", 'Execution output': "```\nNumba is using threading layer workqueue - consider TBB\nfound 1 potential runtime problems - see https://boi.st/lkpy-perf\nEpoch 1: validation_loss = 0.7163\nSeed 1: Recall@20 = 0.2938, NDCG@20 = 0.2837\nEpoch 2: validation_loss = 0.7273\nSeed 7: Recall@20 = 0.2917, NDCG@20 = 0.2727\nEpoch 3: validation_loss = 0.7230\nSeed 21: Recall@20 = 0.2926, NDCG@20 = 0.2770\nEpoch 4: validation_loss = 0.7225\nSeed 42: Recall@20 = 0.2937, NDCG@20 = 0.2775\nEpoch 5: validation_loss = 0.7222\nSeed 84: Recall@20 = 0.2934, NDCG@20 = 0.2778\nEpoch 6: validation_loss = 0.7267\nSeed 123: Recall@20 = 0.2905, NDCG@20 = 0.2733\nEpoch 7: validation_loss = 0.7221\nSeed 256: Recall@20 = 0.2930